WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Translator: Queenie Lee
Reviewer: Elisabeth Buffard

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:12.437
Somewhere deep inside,

00:00:13.217 --> 00:00:16.245
you know what kind of person
you were designed to be.

00:00:18.208 --> 00:00:21.289
If you want to produce great acorns,

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:26.029
think like an oak, not like an acorn.

00:00:26.979 --> 00:00:30.287
Think like the person
you intend to become,

00:00:30.728 --> 00:00:33.538
like the Christian question:
what would Jesus do?

00:00:33.538 --> 00:00:36.648
Ask yourself, how would
the person I'd like to be

00:00:37.308 --> 00:00:39.688
do the things I am about to do.

00:00:40.269 --> 00:00:42.249
The acorn has three parts:

00:00:42.639 --> 00:00:46.429
it's got a stem, a cap, and a seed.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:49.729
And the stem represents
its connection to the past,

00:00:49.729 --> 00:00:51.309
all the acorns, all the oaks

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:55.470
that have ever existed in its line before
are encoded in that,

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:59.720
transferred through that stem,
the legacy into this acorn.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.700
The cap holds onto the seed

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.710
until the seed is ready
to grow on its own,

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:07.580
so the cap represents your coaches,
your mentors, your role models,

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:10.732
your guides, your parents,
your friends, your teachers.

00:01:11.492 --> 00:01:13.460
And when you're ready
to grow on your own,

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.681
the seed of that acorn
holds not only your potential

00:01:17.521 --> 00:01:22.341
but the potential
of every future generation of acorns

00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:24.500
that will spring from that line.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.130
So let me ask you a question.

00:01:27.272 --> 00:01:30.802
What kind of seed is in you?

00:01:33.332 --> 00:01:40.262
See, I believe part of our responsibility
in life is to find out who we are,

00:01:40.262 --> 00:01:41.582
to discover ourselves.

00:01:41.582 --> 00:01:44.622
First off, we need to respect our nature.

00:01:44.622 --> 00:01:48.023
We need to realize
we are part of a continuing chain

00:01:48.023 --> 00:01:51.092
that carries a legacy
and a responsibility.

00:01:51.533 --> 00:01:52.943
And if that's the case,

00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:57.523
then we need to recognize
that we were not biological coincidences.

00:01:58.163 --> 00:02:00.713
I believe there is a creator,

00:02:00.713 --> 00:02:06.553
and I believe you were intentionally
created for a myriad of purposes.

00:02:06.553 --> 00:02:08.811
There are many things
we can do with our lives,

00:02:09.274 --> 00:02:12.019
and I think it's our job to find out
what those things are

00:02:12.019 --> 00:02:14.323
and to do them as well as we possibly can

00:02:14.323 --> 00:02:17.375
so that we're passing
along the right imprint

00:02:17.375 --> 00:02:18.824
for the next generation.

00:02:19.544 --> 00:02:22.949
And that's just simply my life philosophy,
that's the way I look at it.

00:02:22.949 --> 00:02:25.425
So first, we need to respect our nature.

00:02:25.425 --> 00:02:28.975
Second, we need to know our nature.

00:02:29.698 --> 00:02:32.014
Take Aristotle's advice, "Know thyself,"

00:02:32.514 --> 00:02:35.505
but know things about yourself
that most people don't discover.

00:02:35.505 --> 00:02:36.655
For example,

00:02:36.655 --> 00:02:38.445
know how you're smart,

00:02:38.445 --> 00:02:40.946
not just how smart you are
in comparison to others.

00:02:41.276 --> 00:02:42.736
In what ways are you smart?

00:02:42.736 --> 00:02:44.446
Know what you care about.

00:02:44.446 --> 00:02:47.155
What are the values
that motivate your choices?

00:02:47.155 --> 00:02:49.485
Know what your personal velocity is,

00:02:49.485 --> 00:02:53.216
the intensity and drive
with which you naturally operate.

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:56.916
Know the background imprint,
positive, neutral or negative,

00:02:56.916 --> 00:02:58.436
that you carry with you

00:02:58.436 --> 00:03:00.587
and what effect it's had on you.

00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:02.187
Know your behavioral style,

00:03:02.187 --> 00:03:04.367
how you come across to other people.

00:03:04.367 --> 00:03:07.417
Know the patterns in your choices

00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:10.216
so that you're continually
learning more and more

00:03:10.216 --> 00:03:12.547
about what it's like to be you,

00:03:12.907 --> 00:03:15.235
so you can do an even better job of it.

00:03:16.065 --> 00:03:18.837
And then we need to apply our nature,

00:03:18.837 --> 00:03:22.058
we need to nurture our nature
by expressing ourselves in the world.

00:03:22.058 --> 00:03:25.738
See, I never expected
to be anything but ordinary.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:28.288
I was raised to be nice and ordinary.

00:03:28.677 --> 00:03:32.203
I expected I would grow up to be -
my dad worked for the phone company,

00:03:32.203 --> 00:03:34.439
I figured I'd go to work
for the phone company,

00:03:34.439 --> 00:03:36.070
maybe work in an office.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:40.759
I figured I'd work till 65
and have 1.34 kids,

00:03:40.759 --> 00:03:42.609
I'd retire at 65

00:03:42.609 --> 00:03:46.848
and then Iwould die at statistical
average age for my gene pool.

00:03:47.398 --> 00:03:49.059
That's what I expected.

00:03:49.059 --> 00:03:54.530
Until one day in 1972,
on the radio in the next room to mine,

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.469
I heard a voice that changed everything.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.548
I was working for
the Little Rock Housing Authority,

00:04:00.548 --> 00:04:02.829
Little Rock, Arkansas,
urban renewal agency;

00:04:02.829 --> 00:04:05.951
I was a government clerk
making $525 a month;

00:04:05.951 --> 00:04:07.750
I weighed 200 pounds -

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.070
this is 148 -

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:12.180
I smoked two packs of cigarettes a day;

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.111
I'd never set a goal in my life;

00:04:14.111 --> 00:04:16.740
I didn't have a college degree
and no money in the bank;

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:18.991
I was newly married
with a new baby at home;

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.930
and I didn't expect much from life.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:23.131
And in the next room,

00:04:23.131 --> 00:04:25.141
I heard the voice of Earl Nightingale,

00:04:25.141 --> 00:04:28.011
known at the time
as the dean of personal motivation.

00:04:28.464 --> 00:04:30.872
He was on 900 radio stations
around the world,

00:04:30.872 --> 00:04:34.351
and what he said that day
will forever resonate with me.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:40.860
He said, "If you will spend
one extra hour each day

00:04:41.872 --> 00:04:43.711
studying your chosen field,

00:04:44.882 --> 00:04:49.508
you'll be a national expert
in that field in five years or less."

00:04:52.173 --> 00:04:56.202
That hit me like a tornado;
it rearranged everything in my life.

00:04:57.043 --> 00:05:00.573
I started doing the math:
an hour extra a day,

00:05:00.573 --> 00:05:03.093
say five days a week, 50 weeks a year,

00:05:03.093 --> 00:05:05.904
that's 1,250 hours over five years.

00:05:06.294 --> 00:05:11.419
If I spent - me, just ordinary me -
1,250 hours studying one subject ...

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:16.114
Wow! Yeah! I could actually
be a national expert.

00:05:16.114 --> 00:05:18.064
What I want to be an expert at?

00:05:18.064 --> 00:05:20.244
It was not urban renewal.

00:05:20.244 --> 00:05:21.694
(Laughter)

00:05:21.694 --> 00:05:23.605
Then it occurred to me
a few weeks later,

00:05:23.605 --> 00:05:25.844
I want to do what that guy
on the radio's doing.

00:05:25.844 --> 00:05:27.815
But I had no idea what that was.

00:05:27.815 --> 00:05:31.994
I just knew it felt right
to get in the field of human development.

00:05:31.994 --> 00:05:35.215
I thought we'll see, an hour a day,
I am a government clerk.

00:05:35.215 --> 00:05:37.555
I've got eight hours a day.

00:05:37.555 --> 00:05:40.155
(Laughter)

00:05:40.155 --> 00:05:41.965
I could do this by Thursday.

00:05:41.965 --> 00:05:43.255
(Laughter)

00:05:43.255 --> 00:05:45.566
And then I started
thinking about what he'd said,

00:05:45.566 --> 00:05:47.886
and I took him seriously, an hour a day.

00:05:47.886 --> 00:05:50.336
I focused - I thought
I was kind of behind the game,

00:05:50.336 --> 00:05:53.065
so I needed two hours,
and three and four and five.

00:05:53.065 --> 00:05:54.936
So I overcompensated,

00:05:54.936 --> 00:05:58.666
and I became fanatical
about the field of human development.

00:05:58.666 --> 00:06:00.146
And in that five year period,

00:06:00.146 --> 00:06:04.087
I went from being a government clerk
with very little aspiration

00:06:04.087 --> 00:06:06.857
to being a full-time speaker and trainer.

00:06:06.857 --> 00:06:09.236
In two years, that was 1972,

00:06:09.236 --> 00:06:12.736
in 1974, I started buying
Earl Nightingale's training materials

00:06:12.736 --> 00:06:14.987
and selling them to businesses.

00:06:14.987 --> 00:06:21.618
By 1984, his company was selling
my training materials worldwide.

00:06:21.618 --> 00:06:25.339
They sold 3.5 million dollars worth
of one of my first audio albums

00:06:25.339 --> 00:06:27.829
in the first two years it was out.

00:06:27.829 --> 00:06:29.347
I was blown away.

00:06:29.347 --> 00:06:30.768
His formula works,

00:06:30.768 --> 00:06:34.128
and I've seen it work for hundreds
and even thousands of people

00:06:34.128 --> 00:06:37.673
in the many many years since that time
that I've been sharing that message.

00:06:37.673 --> 00:06:39.769
Think about that.
If you were to focus one -

00:06:39.769 --> 00:06:41.677
well, you here, a TED audience -

00:06:41.677 --> 00:06:43.879
if you were to focus half an hour a day,

00:06:43.879 --> 00:06:45.109
(Laughter)

00:06:45.109 --> 00:06:46.188
extra,

00:06:46.188 --> 00:06:49.388
just beyond the TED talk
that you always watch, right?

00:06:49.388 --> 00:06:51.538
Every day, okay, beyond that,

00:06:51.538 --> 00:06:55.619
if you were to focus half an hour of study
on one field of endeavor

00:06:55.619 --> 00:06:57.758
for five consecutive years,

00:06:58.738 --> 00:07:02.879
you'd not only transform you,
you'd transform the world around you.

00:07:02.879 --> 00:07:08.290
And we collectively would transform
the world as we know it today.

00:07:08.869 --> 00:07:13.521
You and I were born with the gift
to make this a better place.

00:07:14.091 --> 00:07:17.451
Even if we didn't improve,
we can make the world better right now.

00:07:17.451 --> 00:07:19.811
We can encourage people,
compliment people,

00:07:19.811 --> 00:07:22.191
we could solve problems,
we could pick up trash,

00:07:22.191 --> 00:07:25.161
we could fix things,
we could bring new ideas.

00:07:25.721 --> 00:07:29.450
But as you grow, you become
a bigger source for the rest of life

00:07:29.450 --> 00:07:31.432
to express itself through you.

00:07:31.832 --> 00:07:33.672
You were put here for a reason.

00:07:34.102 --> 00:07:36.132
It's contained in that acorn.

00:07:36.692 --> 00:07:40.781
So nurture your nature, figure out -

00:07:40.781 --> 00:07:43.663
First off: I am valuable, accept that.

00:07:44.213 --> 00:07:47.007
I want to know who I am,
and I want to know how I operate

00:07:47.007 --> 00:07:48.813
and how can I understand me better.

00:07:48.813 --> 00:07:50.702
And then I want to nurture that nature.

00:07:50.702 --> 00:07:54.073
I want to apply myself in the world
and put myself to work

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:57.572
in such ways that the rest of the world
says: "Well, that's cool.

00:07:57.572 --> 00:08:00.223
If he or she can do it,
I could probably do it.

00:08:00.223 --> 00:08:02.294
I wonder how they did it."

00:08:02.804 --> 00:08:06.323
And then we start spreading that
and the ripple goes worldwide.

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.034
So ask yourself every day,

00:08:09.754 --> 00:08:12.305
how would the person I'd like to be

00:08:13.064 --> 00:08:15.524
do the things I am about to do?

00:08:17.103 --> 00:08:18.144
Thank you.

00:08:18.144 --> 00:08:21.025
(Applause)

